{{/*
Copyright The OpenTelemetry Authors
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

Template for the RPM spec that builds every component, rendered by
WriteSpec in spec.go. Text outside the {{...}} actions is emitted verbatim,
so this file reads as the spec it produces.

Two escaping rules apply to the text below, both of them rpm's:

  - Never write a section macro (install, files, changelog, and so on) with a
    leading percent sign inside a comment. Rpm expands macros in comments too,
    and an unescaped section macro in a comment above the preamble makes rpm
    4.16 (EL9) start that section mid-comment and swallow the preamble.
  - Percent signs in interpolated data are escaped by the generator, not here;
    the inlined lifecycle scripts arrive with their percent signs doubled.
